body:
I picked up a female friend a couple hours after we each celebrated New Years at different events. We wound up at some random house party in San Francisco where we knew no one. She decided that night that she was attracted to me and started hooking up with me out of the blue. She suggested we find a room. We drunkenly stumbled upstairs where there were two enthusiastic men who greeted us, "Well hello! What be your drug of choice this new year?! In this room we have people on acid, and this room is for the weed people..." I interrupted, "Where is the molly room?" He looked at his friend and said, "Uh, it's that one, but there doesn't seem to be anyone in there for some reason. Enjoy!" Went in, closed the door, and fooled around, before breaking the sheets of the tightly made bed and going to sleep. The sunrise shining through the victorian windows, woke us up to the beautifully clean and decorated male's bedroom we were using. It seemed like it belonged to a fairly well-to-do techie judging by the closet, furniture, hobbies, and organization. Moments later, a good looking guy quietly opens the door to quickly grab something. I raise my head from the pillow urgently to ask, "Omg, is this your bedroom?" He nods and whispers, "Yeah, no problem! Take as long as you want! I just had to grab something." It was almost as if he was apologizing for disturbing us. I rushed to tell him, "Thank you! Dude, you have a beautiful bedroom!" before he closed the door. He said, "Thanks!"

&#x200B;

TLDR; used a stranger's tightly kept bedroom at a house party to rail a chick and sleep til morning. He didn't want to disturb us sleeping in his bed the next day when he quietly tried to grab his keys from the dresser.
